  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1}\n  [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n  (b a : ℝ),\n  0 ≤ b →\n    0 < a →\n      ∃ T H B,\n        ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel T ∧\n          ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel H ∧\n            ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel B ∧\n              (∀ (u : E), T u = μ.tilted fun x => -(b / 2) * ‖x - u‖ ^ 2) ∧\n                (∀ (u : E),\n                    H u = AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing (T u) √a) ∧\n                  (∀ (u y : E),\n                      B (u, y) = MeasureTheory.Measure.map (Prod.mk u) ((T u).tilted fun x => -‖x - y‖ ^ 2 / (2 * a))) ∧\n                    (∀ (u y : E),\n                        B (u, y) =\n                          MeasureTheory.Measure.map (Prod.mk u)\n                            (μ.tilted fun x => -((b + a⁻¹) / 2) * ‖x - (b + a⁻¹)⁻¹ • (b • u + a⁻¹ • y)‖ ^ 2)) ∧\n                      ∀ (ν : MeasureTheory.Measure E), MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure ν → ⇑B ∘ₘ ν ⊗ₘ H = ν ⊗ₘ T",
    "statement_sha256": "c850e86a9361203666d0048bd15d35ebef0a79b5234cb9e5d0932caad7a72790",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "Measure E is a countably additive Borel measure. IsProbabilityMeasure means total mass one. Kernel X Y is a jointly parameter-measurable assignment x to a measure on Y; IsMarkovKernel means every fiber has total mass one.",
      "mu.tilted(f) is the measure with density exp(f) divided by its integral against mu. The statement supplies no extra moment or density hypothesis.",
      "GaussianSmoothing.gaussianSmoothing(P,s) is the actual law of X+sZ under P times the centered identity-covariance standard Gaussian on E. Its parameter is a standard-deviation scale.",
      "Measure.map(f,P) is the pushforward of P under f. Prod.mk u is the map x to (u,x). Norms and scalar multiplication are those of the real inner-product space.",
      "nu compProd H, written nu ⊗ₘ H, is the actual joint law with first-coordinate distribution nu and second-coordinate conditional kernel H: its value at measurable S is integral H(u)({y | (u,y) in S}) dnu(u). B composed with a measure M, written B ∘ₘ M, is its bind: value at measurable S is integral B(z)(S) dM(z). In the printed statement T and H have type Kernel E E, and B has type Kernel (E times E) (E times E)."
    ]
  },
